From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uiautomationcore: cached children and parent

A cache request may now have TreeScope_Children and TreeScope_Descendants
(put_TreeScope refused them; the scope is stored as given and the request
sent to the providers also covers the element). The elements a cache request
returns for such a scope remember the cached tree: GetCachedChildren answers
the children cached for the element (an empty array when it has none, in
tree order), GetCachedParent the cached parent, and an element whose request
did not cover them answers E_INVALIDARG. The tree is shared by its elements,
so it outlives the element the request was made for. Removes the two
todo_wine marks of the cache request scope test.
---
